From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:19:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: use atomic RX buffer allocations


Use alloc_skb for RX replenishment rather than dev_alloc_skb. This is
a buffer allocation policy change, including headroom and page-fragment
behavior; it is not a fix for an unmatched free.
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -371,8 +371,8 @@ int ath11k_dp_rxbufs_replenish(struct at
 	num_remain = req_entries;
 
 	while (num_remain > 0) {
-		skb = dev_alloc_skb(DP_RX_BUFFER_SIZE +
-				    DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE);
+		skb = alloc_skb(DP_RX_BUFFER_SIZE +
+				DP_RX_BUFFER_ALIGN_SIZE, GFP_ATOMIC);
 		if (!skb)
 			break;
 
